.TH CCOL_DYNAMIC_QUEUE_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_dynamic_queue_destroy \- destroy a dynamic queue
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_dynamic_queue_destroy(dq);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees all resources associated with the queue. The queue pointer is
automatically set to NULL after destruction.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
dq   Dynamic queue to destroy (will be set to NULL)
.fi
.SH WARNINGS
.nf
Messages remaining in the queue cause assertion failure
Drain the queue before destroying
A ccol_select()/ccol_select_timed() call or a ccol_event_loop registration
(ccol_selectable_from_dynq/ccol_selectable_from_chan) still watching this queue
also causes assertion failure; the still-linked waiter would otherwise
reference this queue's own, about-to-be-freed mutex
Call ccol_event_loop_remove(), or let every watching ccol_select()/
ccol_select_timed() call return, before destroying
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with NULL pointer
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_dynamic_queue_create (3),
.BR __ccol_dynamic_queue_destroy (3)
